-- s 23(2): the most in interim payments: 3% of the single-offence maximum, funeral payments aside.
#ASSERT `Most in interim payments question` `Sam was punched` TRUE EQUALS `answered` 2250
#ASSERT `Most in interim payments question` (`the day` 31 12 2003) TRUE EQUALS `answered` 1500
#ASSERT `Most in interim payments question` (`the day` 1 6 1980) TRUE EQUALS `answered` 225
#ASSERT `Most in interim payments question` (`the day` 1 6 1972) TRUE EQUALS `answered` 60
#ASSERT `Most in interim payments question` (`the day` 1 6 1972) FALSE EQUALS `answered` 9
#ASSERT `Most in interim payments question` (`the day` 1 6 1970) TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `the Act does not apply to an offence committed before 22 January 1971 (s 8), so it sets no maximum`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- How much will I be paid. Arguments: applying as, date of offence, indictable, the offences, date applied, just amount,
-- examination cost, interim payments, private health insurer, already received, assessor deducts for what will be
-- received, Fatal Accidents Act part, owed to the State, set off.
-- The assessor would think $100 000 just; the maximum is $75 000.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid question` `victim` `Sam was punched` TRUE `single` (`the day` 1 6 2024) 100000 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 75000
-- Exactly at the maximum, and just over it.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid question` `victim` `Sam was punched` TRUE `single` (`the day` 1 6 2024) 75000 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 75000
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid question` `victim` `Sam was punched` TRUE `single` (`the day` 1 6 2024) 75001 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 75000
-- $40 000 just, less examination $1 000, interim $2 000, health insurer $500, received $3 000, to be received $1 500:
-- 40 000 - 8 000 = 32 000.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid question` `victim` `Sam was punched` TRUE `single` (`the day` 1 6 2024) 40000 1000 2000 500 3000 1500 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 32000
-- The maximum first, then the deductions: $100 000 just, interim $2 250, received $10 000: 75 000 - 12 250 = 62 750.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid question` `victim` `Sam was punched` TRUE `single` (`the day` 1 6 2024) 100000 0 2250 0 10000 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 62750
-- s 42(5): the executor claims $60 000 for Lee's widow; she has received $50 000, of which $40 000 is life insurance of
-- the Fatal Accidents Act s 5(2)(b) kind: only $10 000 is deducted: 50 000.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid question` `representative` `Sam was punched` TRUE `single` (`the day` 1 6 2024) 60000 0 0 0 50000 0 40000 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 50000
-- The same figures for an injured victim: s 42(5) does not help, so all $50 000 is deducted: 10 000.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid question` `victim` `Sam was punched` TRUE `single` (`the day` 1 6 2024) 60000 0 0 0 50000 0 40000 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 10000
-- s 43: owes $5 000; the assessor sets off $8 000, but not more than is owed: 30 000 - 5 000 = 25 000. Sets off $3 000: 27 000.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid question` `victim` `Sam was punched` TRUE `single` (`the day` 1 6 2024) 30000 0 0 0 0 0 0 5000 8000 EQUALS `answered` 25000
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid question` `victim` `Sam was punched` TRUE `single` (`the day` 1 6 2024) 30000 0 0 0 0 0 0 5000 3000 EQUALS `answered` 27000
-- Deductions larger than the award: nothing is paid.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid question` `victim` `Sam was punched` TRUE `single` (`the day` 1 6 2024) 5000 0 0 0 9000 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 0
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid question` `victim` (`the day` 1 1 1970) TRUE `single` (`the day` 1 6 2024) 5000 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `not covered` `the Act does not apply to an offence committed before 22 January 1971 (s 8), so it sets no maximum`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 47: when can I be paid. Award on 1 June 2026; the 21 days of s 55(3) end on 22 June 2026.
#ASSERT `When can I be paid question` (`the day` 1 6 2026) (`the day` 22 6 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: payment waits until the 21 days for an appeal have elapsed (s 47(a), s 55(3))` (`the day` 22 6 2026)
#ASSERT `When can I be paid question` (`the day` 1 6 2026) (`the day` 23 6 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `now: the 21 days for an appeal have elapsed and no appeal is awaiting decision (s 47)`
#ASSERT `When can I be paid question` (`the day` 1 6 2026) (`the day` 2 6 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `now: an assessor has given written authority for payment (s 47)`
#ASSERT `When can I be paid question` (`the day` 1 6 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: payment waits until the appeal is determined (s 47(b))`
#ASSERT `When can I be paid question` (`the day` 1 6 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `now: the 21 days for an appeal have elapsed and no appeal is awaiting decision (s 47)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 55: can I appeal. Decision on 1 June 2026; the 21 days end on 22 June 2026.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal question` `the amount of the award` (`the day` 1 6 2026) (`the day` 22 6 2026) EQUALS `answered` (`yes, in time: I may appeal to the District Court; the appeal must be commenced by the last day of the 21 days (s 55(1), (3)); its decision is final (s 57)` (`the day` 22 6 2026))
#ASSERT `Can I appeal question` `the decision to make, or to refuse to make, an award` (`the day` 1 6 2026) (`the day` 23 6 2026) EQUALS `answered` (`late: the 21 days have ended; the District Court may allow the appeal to be commenced if it is just to do so (s 55(4)); its decision is final (s 57)` (`the day` 22 6 2026))
#ASSERT `Can I appeal question` `some other decision (for example to defer, stay or require me to take other proceedings)` (`the day` 1 6 2026) (`the day` 2 6 2026) EQUALS `not covered` `section 55(1) gives the applicant an appeal against a decision to make or refuse an award, and as to its amount; this Act does not speak to an appeal against other decisions`
-- The s 55 rule: day 0 is the decision.
`I appeal on day 21` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 55 -- appeal within 21 days, or the District Court may allow it later` 0 (LIST (EVENT `I, the applicant` `commence an appeal to the District Court` 21))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `I appeal on day 21` EQUALS TRUE
`I appeal on day 22` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 55 -- appeal within 21 days, or the District Court may allow it later` 0 (LIST (EVENT `I, the applicant` `commence an appeal to the District Court` 22))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `I appeal on day 22` EQUALS FALSE
`I appeal late and the Court allows it` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 55 -- appeal within 21 days, or the District Court may allow it later` 0 (LIST (EVENT `I, the applicant` `commence an appeal to the District Court` 22), (EVENT `the District Court` `allow the appeal to be commenced after the 21 days` 40))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `I appeal late and the Court allows it` EQUALS TRUE
#TRACE `s 55 -- appeal within 21 days, or the District Court may allow it later` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `I, the applicant` DOES `commence an appeal to the District Court` AT 22
-- expect: not BREACH: the residual permission, PARTY the District Court MAY allow the appeal to be commenced after the 21 days

