-- s 48: future treatment money. Arguments: date of birth, date of award, date of request.
-- Born 1 January 2000, award at 10 (1 January 2010): before turning 28, so by 31 December 2027 (later than 31 July 2018).
#ASSERT `Can I still ask for future treatment money question` (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 1 1 2010) (`the day` 31 12 2027) EQUALS `yes: give the Chief Assessor the request, with evidence that the treatment expenses were reasonably incurred as a direct consequence of the injury, by the last day (s 48(1), (2))` (`the day` 31 12 2027)
#ASSERT `Can I still ask for future treatment money question` (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 1 1 2010) (`the day` 1 1 2028) EQUALS `no: the time to give the request ended, so the amount for future treatment is not to be paid (s 48(1)(c), (2))` (`the day` 31 12 2027)
-- Born 1 January 1985, award at 17 (1 January 2002): 28 on 1 January 2013, but 31 July 2018 is later.
#ASSERT `Can I still ask for future treatment money question` (`the day` 1 1 1985) (`the day` 1 1 2002) (`the day` 31 7 2018) EQUALS `yes: give the Chief Assessor the request, with evidence that the treatment expenses were reasonably incurred as a direct consequence of the injury, by the last day (s 48(1), (2))` (`the day` 31 7 2018)
#ASSERT `Can I still ask for future treatment money question` (`the day` 1 1 1985) (`the day` 1 1 2002) (`the day` 1 8 2018) EQUALS `no: the time to give the request ended, so the amount for future treatment is not to be paid (s 48(1)(c), (2))` (`the day` 31 7 2018)
-- Award on the 18th birthday (5 May 2018): not under 18, so 10 years from the award: 5 May 2028. The day before: under 18,
-- so the day before the 28th birthday: 4 May 2028.
#ASSERT `Can I still ask for future treatment money question` (`the day` 5 5 2000) (`the day` 5 5 2018) (`the day` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `yes: give the Chief Assessor the request, with evidence that the treatment expenses were reasonably incurred as a direct consequence of the injury, by the last day (s 48(1), (2))` (`the day` 5 5 2028)
#ASSERT `Can I still ask for future treatment money question` (`the day` 5 5 2000) (`the day` 4 5 2018) (`the day` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `yes: give the Chief Assessor the request, with evidence that the treatment expenses were reasonably incurred as a direct consequence of the injury, by the last day (s 48(1), (2))` (`the day` 4 5 2028)
-- Adults: an award before 31 July 2008 (1 January 2005): 31 July 2018. On 31 July 2008: 10 years from the award, also
-- 31 July 2018. On 1 August 2008: 1 August 2018.
#ASSERT `Can I still ask for future treatment money question` (`the day` 1 1 1970) (`the day` 1 1 2005) (`the day` 1 8 2018) EQUALS `no: the time to give the request ended, so the amount for future treatment is not to be paid (s 48(1)(c), (2))` (`the day` 31 7 2018)
#ASSERT `Can I still ask for future treatment money question` (`the day` 1 1 1970) (`the day` 31 7 2008) (`the day` 1 1 2010) EQUALS `yes: give the Chief Assessor the request, with evidence that the treatment expenses were reasonably incurred as a direct consequence of the injury, by the last day (s 48(1), (2))` (`the day` 31 7 2018)
#ASSERT `Can I still ask for future treatment money question` (`the day` 1 1 1970) (`the day` 1 8 2008) (`the day` 1 8 2018) EQUALS `yes: give the Chief Assessor the request, with evidence that the treatment expenses were reasonably incurred as a direct consequence of the injury, by the last day (s 48(1), (2))` (`the day` 1 8 2018)

