-- ss 23(4), 68: what I may have to pay back. Arguments: interim payments, refused, amount awarded, received otherwise,
-- deducted, reduced because of the award.
#ASSERT `What must I pay back question` 2000 TRUE 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `What must I pay back question` 0 FALSE 50000 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- Sam is awarded $50 000, then wins $20 000 damages from the offender in a civil claim that took no account of the award.
#ASSERT `What must I pay back question` 0 FALSE 50000 20000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 20000
-- Damages of $80 000: the lesser is the award, $50 000.
#ASSERT `What must I pay back question` 0 FALSE 50000 80000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `What must I pay back question` 0 FALSE 50000 20000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What must I pay back question` 0 FALSE 50000 20000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0

